    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6c3791e8-6b2d-5a26-b6c7-64983f693e44",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 11 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -10 \\\\ -7 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 11 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 5 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
