      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $E$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -11 \\\\ 7 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
